# Code owners.
#
# Two jobs:
#   1. GitHub auto-requests review from the matching owner on every PR.
#   2. scripts/ci/review-policy.sh reads the '*' catch-all to decide who is
#      allowed to approve an outside contributor's PR. That is the single source
#      of truth for "who is a maintainer" — keep it accurate.
#
# NOTE: `require_code_owner_review` is deliberately NOT enabled on the main
# ruleset. With one maintainer who is also the sole code owner, it would demand
# an approval only that person can give, and GitHub forbids approving your own
# PR — making every maintainer PR permanently unmergeable. Add a second
# maintainer here BEFORE turning that switch on.

# Catch-all
*                       @darisadam

# Per-area, so delegation later is a one-line change
/backend/               @darisadam
/web/                   @darisadam
/mobile/                @darisadam
/deploy/                @darisadam
/docs/                  @darisadam

# Governance, security and CI: intentionally listed separately so a future
# maintainer set does not silently inherit control of the enforcement machinery.
/.github/               @darisadam
/.github/workflows/     @darisadam
/.github/CODEOWNERS     @darisadam
/scripts/               @darisadam
/SECURITY.md            @darisadam
/.gitleaks.toml         @darisadam
/.gitleaksignore        @darisadam
/osv-scanner.toml       @darisadam
/LICENSE                @darisadam
/NOTICE                 @darisadam
/TRADEMARKS.md          @darisadam
